INT. CURLING CLUB - SHEET THREE - EVENING

Pebbled ice, humming compressors. A scoreboard reads: ROCKS FALLING, HOUSE TIED.

COACH MARGUERITE LAVOIE (50s, club jacket, whistle) watches from the hack. Skip BJORN HALLDORSSON (40s, broom, one-glove) kneels in the house, calling the line. Third DESMOND "DEZ" ARCHER (20s, jittery) cradles a stone. Second WILHELMINA "WILLA" NG (30s, goggles) sweeps beside it. Lead TAMSIN OKORO (20s, ponytail) holds the broom. And ALTERNATE POPPY DUNLEAVY (teen, coat zipped to chin) sits on the bench, gripping her knees.

BJORN
Dez, hold.

DEZ
Holding.

Marguerite does not speak. Her eyes move from Dez to the stone to Poppy and back.

BJORN
Easy weight.

Dez releases. The stone glides. Willa and Tamsin sweep in sync, the sound of brooms like rain.

WILLA
Hard!

TAMSIN
Hurry hard!

The stone slows. Poppy leans forward. It curls, kisses the guard, and stops one inch from the button.

Silence. Then Marguerite lowers her whistle, takes a breath, and sits down next to Poppy.

MARGUERITE
(quietly)
You're up next.

Poppy swallows. Nods. Stands. Takes off her coat. Underneath: the jersey, a size too large. She picks up a stone.

Behind her, the whole team watches. She walks to the hack.
